-- title:
--   One-place enlargement of a quaternion order at a split place
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense used here: $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module. Let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, with completion $\mathbb{Q}_v$ and valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v$, and let $\varphi : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v \to M_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$ be a ring isomorphism which is normalised on scalars, i.e. $\varphi(1\otimes r) = r\cdot I_2$ for all $r\in\mathbb{Q}_v$. Let $h\in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_v)$. Write $\Lambda_v$ for the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c\in\mathcal{O}_v$. Assume that for every $x\in\Lambda_v$ all entries of $h^{-1}\varphi(x)h$ lie in $\mathcal{O}_v$. Then there is a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $\Lambda'$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is again an order in the above sense, contains $\Lambda$, and satisfies: for every $x\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$, $x$ lies in the corresponding additive subgroup $\Lambda'_v$ if and only if all entries of $h^{-1}\varphi(x)h$ lie in $\mathcal{O}_v$; that is, $\Lambda'_v = \varphi^{-1}\bigl(h\,M_2(\mathcal{O}_v)\,h^{-1}\bigr)$.
--
--   This is the one-place enlargement step in the theory of orders in a quaternion algebra: an order whose local box at a split place $v$ is contained in a conjugate of $M_2(\mathcal{O}_v)$ can be enlarged, without changing anything at the other places, to an order whose box at $v$ is exactly that conjugate. It feeds the characterisation of the local boxes of maximal orders at split places used in the Eichler-order input to the argument.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_exists_isOrder_le_localBox_iff_conj_apply_mem_adicCompletionIntegers.lean

